g and performance on an organization's mission-critical priorities in the United States, Canada, Europe, the Middle East, Africa, and internationally. It operates through three segments: Insights, Conferences, and Consulting. The Insights segment delivers insights through subscription services, such as access to published content, data and benchmarks, and direct access to a network of business and technology experts. The Conferences segment enables executives and teams to learn, share, and network through its Symposium/Xpo series and peer-driven sessions, as well as through its conferences focused on specific business roles and topics. The Consulting segment provides technology-driven strategic initiatives, including custom analysis and on-the-ground support to senior executives. This segment also offers actionable solutions for IT-related priorities, including IT cost optimization, digital transformation, and IT sourcing optimization. The company was formerly known as Gartner Group, Inc. and changed its name to Gartner, Inc. in November 2001. Gartner, Inc. was founded in 1979 and is headquartered in Stamford, Connecticut.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Eugene A. Hall | CEO & Chairman | Age 68 | Compensation: $2.6M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 19K people. Revenue per employee of $334K ranks in the below the sector median among Technology peers, with revenue growing 11%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $60K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $8K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 8\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Gartner, Inc. is a large-cap technology business with a $11.0B market cap on $6.5B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +6% over the past three years and +12% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 45% against a 9% cost of capital \u2014 a 36-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat. Gross margins of 61% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $1.2B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 18 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.77\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 8.2\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 18.1% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 2.7% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (14.1% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 8% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Technology ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (43% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Sector under pressure with a 19.3% decline over the past 6 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 9% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 64% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 43% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Technology peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Deloitte named a Leader in the 2026 Gartner Magic Quadrant\u2122 for Software Asset Management Managed Services","source":"prnewswire.com","link":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/deloitte-named-a-leader-in-the-2026-gartner-magic-quadrant-for-software-asset-management-managed-services-302946455.html","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795190400.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.612,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Executives get more AI training than other workers, hurting adoption, report finds","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/technology/ai/articles/executives-more-ai-training-other-210700241.html","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795208820.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.402,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"QNT & QBTS: 2 Quantum Stocks to Buy for Triple-Digit Growth in 2027","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/technology/ai/articles/qnt-qbts-2-quantum-stocks-190000464.html","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795201200.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.649,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":["m_and_a"]},{"title":"Bigger AI models aren\u2019t always better","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/bigger-ai-models-aren-t-180101000.html","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795198090.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.44,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Sprocket Security Named a